{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Yoreh.</b> It is the first rainfall that descends in Marcheshvan, and it is called yoreh because it instructs (מורה) people to plaster their roofs. Another explanation: because it shoots (יורה) like an arrow." "<b>And malkosh.</b> In Nisan, and it is called malkosh because it fills (ממלא) the grain in its stalks." "<b>ואספת דגנך.</b> That is, afterwards rains would not descend, because it is the time of gathering and harvest, and rain at the time of harvest is a sign of curse, as it is said: ״הלא קציר חטים היום״ etc. And in tractate Berakhot it asks: it is written ואספת, which implies you yourself, and it is written ״ועמדו זרים ורעו צאנכם״? And it answers: here, at a time when Israel does the will of the Omnipresent; here, when they do not do the will of the Omnipresent. And it is difficult, for behold it stands on ״והיה אם שמוע״, and this requires investigation."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:51.685279266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}